--
Reclassified as KNOWNBUG by the member-alias template-parameter identity fix
(template_map.cpp, per [temp.local]/1).  That fix makes std::decay /
std::__conditional resolve correctly, which reroutes std::make_tuple/std::get's
member instantiation through the lazy, ODR-use-driven path; a member body that
yields a type-trait result is not instantiated there, leaving a decltype
unresolved ("expected type, but got expression" at the std::get<0> use).
Pre-existing gap in ODR-use-driven member-function instantiation
([temp.inst]/4 + [basic.def.odr]) hidden by the eager-substitution path; tracked
as Part 2 (.kiro/part2_findings.md).
